  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal fails to overcome the concerns identified in the previous refusal. It would continue by reason of its siting, size, width, scale, massing and overall design to result in an incongruous visually prominent form of development which would fail to harmonise with the character and architectural composition of the surrounding properties.",
    "This would result in a visually dominant building which would be detrimental to the character, appearance and visual amenity of the street scene and the setting of Ickenham Village Conservation Area. The limited public benefits would not outweigh the harm to the Ickenham Village Conservation Area. The proposal therefore conflicts with Policies BE1 and HE1 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part One - Strategic Policies (2012), Policies DMHB1, DMHB4, DMHB11 and DMHB12 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part Two - Development Management Policies (2020), Policy HC1 of the London Plan (2021), Section 72(1) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Ar",
    "The proposal fails to overcome the concerns identified in the previous refusal and would continue due to its depth, scale, bulk, siting and overall design, to have an overbearing impact on the adjoining residents leading to a harmful sense of enclosure and loss of outlook to the residents of Nos 88 and 92 Long Lane.The proposal therefore conflicts with Policy BE1 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part One - Strategic Policies (2012), Policy DMHB11 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part Two - Development Management Policies (2020) and the National Planning Policy Framework (2026)."
  ],
